latvia takes the penultimate step toward  joining euro single currency area this  week at talks in brussels EU finance and  economy ministers aim to adopt the last  three legislative files needed for the  Baltic state to join the euro climate  among their decisions The ministers will  rubber-stamp rules setting a permanent  conversion rate for the Latvian money  that lat against the euro it will all  pave the way for Latvia to become the  18th eurozone nation on january 1st 2014  during the meeting the council will  discuss the new Lithuanian presidencies  work program in economic and financial  affairs for the next six months while  keeping up Europe's focus on growth and  jobs the presidency has set further  development of the banking Union as a  key priority to help ensure EU financial  stability it regards the single  resolution mechanism for dealing with  failing banks as the next important step  in that process presidency also wants to  work toward ensuring sound transparent  and resilient financial markets and to  strengthen the protection of investors  in Europe other items on the minister's  agenda include the expected endorsement  of three documents for implementing the  so-called 2-pack of economic governance  rules
 

